[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 764,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 701,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119118,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 701,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Mixed-phenotype acute leukaemia (MPAL) with <em>KMT2A</em> rearrangement is an acute leukaemia that fulfils the criteria for MPAL and in which the <em>KMT2A</em> locus on chromosome 11q23.3 is fused with any of a number of partner genes.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:13:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 765,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 702,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119119,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 702,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>9807/3 Mixed-phenotype acute leukaemia with <em>KMT2A</em> rearrangement</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:13:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 766,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 703,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119120,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 703,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>2A61 &amp; XH2S51 Acute leukaemias of ambiguous lineage &amp; Mixed-phenotype acute leukaemia with t(v;11q23); <em>MLL</em>-rearranged</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:13:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 767,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 704,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119121,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 704,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> mixed-phenotype acute leukaemia with <em>MLL</em> rearrangement.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:13:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 768,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 705,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119122,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 705,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:13:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 769,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 706,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119123,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 706,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Bone marrow and peripheral blood are always involved. Some patients present with myeloid sarcoma.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:13:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 770,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 707,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119124,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 707,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Patients present with clinical features similar to those of other acute leukaemias, typically secondary to cytopenias. This MPAL type has no distinctive clinical features.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:13:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 771,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 708,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119125,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 708,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>This MPAL type is rare. It is more common in children than in adults, and within the former age group it is relatively more common in infancy {10457405; 16437134; 21228332}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:13:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 772,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 709,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119126,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 709,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:13:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 773,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 710,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119127,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 710,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>The cell of origin is probably a haematopoietic stem cell or progenitor cell with lineage plasticity {30209392}. <em>KMT2A</em>gene rearrangements result from deletions, duplications, inversions, and translocations at the 11q23 locus {10468849}. These rearrangements typically disrupt a 100&nbsp;kb region in exons&nbsp;5&ndash;11. The resulting derivative chromosome&nbsp;11 harbours the <em>KMT2A</em> promoter and coding regions 5&prime;&nbsp;to the breakpoint {10468849}. The rearrangement results in a chimeric protein with a <em>KMT2A</em>-encoded N-terminus and a C-terminus encoded by the partner gene {10468849}. The most common 5&prime;&nbsp;<em>KMT2A</em> partners in MPAL are <em>AFF1</em> (<em>AF4</em>) at 4q21, <em>MLLT3</em> (<em>AF9</em>) at 9p22, and <em>MLLT1</em> (<em>ENL</em>) at 19p13 {23888868; 30209392}. MPAL with <em>KMT2A</em> rearrangement has a low mutation burden and classically has few copy-number alterations {30209392}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:13:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 780,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 717,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119128,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 717,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:13:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 774,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 711,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119129,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 711,
        "headingText": "<p>Peripheral blood smears and bone marrow aspirate smears often show a dimorphic blast population, with some blasts resembling monoblasts/promonocytes and others resembling lymphoblasts. Some cases have only one dominant blast morphology, or undifferentiated blasts. Most cases present extensive blast infiltration, but in rare instances blasts may be &lt;&nbsp;20% of cells in the bone marrow and peripheral blood.</p>\r\n\r\n<h5>Immunophenotype</h5>\r\n\r\n<p>MPAL with <em>KMT2A</em> rearrangement usually has a B/myeloid immunophenotype {26276768}. Rare cases of acute undifferentiated leukaemia with <em>KMT2A</em> rearrangement, as well as MPAL with combined B/T&nbsp;lineage, have also been described {21228332; 22581002; 32372024}. Commonly expressed myeloid antigens include CD11b, CD13, CD15, CD25, CD65, KIT (CD117), myeloperoxidase, and lysozyme. Commonly expressed lymphoid antigens include CD2, CD7, CD19, CD22, cCD22, and cCD79a. CD10 is usually negative in the B-lymphoblastic component. CD56 may be expressed {19131545; 21228332}.</p>\r\n&nbsp;",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:14:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 775,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 712,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119130,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 712,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>See above.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:13:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 776,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 713,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119131,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 713,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Detection of <em>KMT2A</em> rearrangements may be accomplished using conventional karyotyping. However, some <em>KMT2A</em>rearrangements can be cytogenetically cryptic and require alternative techniques for detection, such as FISH or RNA sequencing. Complex rearrangements, particularly <em>KMT2A</em>::<em>USP2</em>, may be undetectable by FISH {30899083; 32196814; 32372024}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:13:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 779,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 716,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119132,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 716,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> increased blasts in bone marrow and/or blood with an immunophenotype that meets the diagnostic criteria for MPAL (may be &lt;&nbsp;20%); presence of a <em>KMT2A</em> rearrangement; no history of exposure to cytotoxic therapy.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> identification of the <em>KMT2A</em> fusion partner.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:13:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 777,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 714,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119133,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 714,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:13:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 778,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 715,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119134,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 715,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Outcome data on cases classified using contemporary MPAL criteria are limited. Anecdotal reports describe this MPAL type as a high-risk disease with poor survival even in younger patients {29720486; 32419244}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:13:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]